From: atomchild411 <143453386+atomchild411@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] WTF: IRIX thread-key sentinel is a constant

IRIX's limits.h defines PTHREAD_KEYS_MAX as _sysconf(104), so it cannot
initialise the constexpr InvalidThreadSpecificKey.  IRIX pthread keys
are ints counted from 0; use -1.
---
--- a/Source/WTF/wtf/ThreadingPrimitives.h
+++ b/Source/WTF/wtf/ThreadingPrimitives.h
@@ -116,7 +116,13 @@
 
 #if USE(PTHREADS)
 
+#if OS(IRIX)
+// IRIX's PTHREAD_KEYS_MAX is a _sysconf() call, not a constant.  Keys are
+// ints counted from 0, so -1 is never a valid one.
+static constexpr ThreadSpecificKey InvalidThreadSpecificKey = -1;
+#else
 static constexpr ThreadSpecificKey InvalidThreadSpecificKey = PTHREAD_KEYS_MAX;
+#endif
 
 inline void threadSpecificKeyCreate(ThreadSpecificKey* key, void (*destructor)(void *))
 {
